00:51:43,448 --> 00:51:49,448
Big Fish is a 2003 American fantasy drama film directed by Tim Burton.

13
00:56:02,068 --> 00:56:08,068
It is based on the 1998 novel Big Fish: A Novel of
Mythic Proportions by Daniel Wallace.

14
01:00:20,689 --> 01:00:26,689
The film stars Ewan McGregor, Albert Finney, Billy Crudup, Jessica Lange, Helena Bonham Carter,
Alison Lohman, Robert Guillaume, Marion Cotillard, Steve Buscemi, and Danny DeVito.

15
01:04:39,310 --> 01:04:45,310
It tells the story of a frustrated son who tries to distinguish fact from
fiction in the life of his father, a teller of tall tales.

16
01:08:57,931 --> 01:09:03,931
The film's screenwriter, John August, read a manuscript of the novel six months before
it was published and convinced Columbia Pictures to acquire the rights.

17
01:13:16,551 --> 01:13:22,551
He began adapting the novel as a screenplay while producers negotiated with Steven Spielberg about
directing the film; Spielberg eventually left the project to focus on Catch Me If You Can (2002).

18
01:17:35,172 --> 01:17:41,172
Tim Burton and Richard D.

19
01:21:53,793 --> 01:21:59,793
Zanuck took over after completing Planet of the Apes (2001),
and brought McGregor and Finney on board.

20
01:26:12,413 --> 01:26:18,413
The film's theme of reconciliation between a dying father and his son had
special significance for Burton, whose father had died in 2000.

21
01:30:31,034 --> 01:30:37,034
Big Fish was shot on location in Alabama in a series of fairy
tale vignettes with a Southern Gothic aesthetic.

22
01:34:49,655 --> 01:34:55,655
The film premiered on December 4, 2003 in Manhattan.

23
01:39:08,275 --> 01:39:14,275
It was released in limited capacity on December 10,
followed by a wide release on January 9, 2004.

24
01:43:26,896 --> 01:43:32,896
It received various award nominations, including seven BAFTA nominations,
four Golden Globe nominations and two Saturn Award nominations.

25
01:47:45,517 --> 01:47:51,517
It also received an Academy Award nomination and a Grammy Award
nomination for Danny Elfman's original score.

26
01:52:04,137 --> 01:52:10,137
A musical adaptation of Big Fish premiered in Chicago in April 2013.

27
01:56:22,758 --> 01:56:28,758
The film explores themes of witch, fish, love of one's
life, parent child relationship, circus.

28
02:00:41,379 --> 02:00:47,379
The tone is emotional.
